+# Daily Grind performance audit
+
+Audited on 2026-11-11. Scope: the repository's single static page, `index.html`, and its hero image. No browser, development/preview server, or server entrypoint was used. There is no production build script; the HTML and assets are ready to serve directly.
+
+## Findings and changes
+
+| Area | Finding | Change / assessment |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| LCP: discovery | The hero was a CSS background without a preload or priority hint. Its request depended on CSS processing. | Put the hero in the initial HTML as an eager, high-priority `<img>`. The preload scanner can discover it directly. A separate preload is unnecessary for this small, inline-styled document. |
+| LCP: transfer | Every viewport requested the same 1350px remote image. | Self-hosted four WebP sizes with `srcset` and `sizes`. The sizing accounts for `object-fit: cover`, the 60vh hero, and its 300px minimum height. Only the chosen candidate is downloaded. |
+| Connection overhead | The only critical image required a connection to `images.unsplash.com`. | All page resources now use the same origin. No third-party DNS/TLS connection is required to render the page. |
+| CLS | The hero already had a fixed viewport-relative height; the image change must preserve its space. | Kept the 60vh section, added a minimum height, and set intrinsic image dimensions. The absolute image cannot move surrounding content when it loads. The dark overlay and original crop behavior remain. |
+| INP | No scripts, listeners, hydration, timers, third-party widgets, or JavaScript long tasks exist in this repository. | Preserved zero runtime JavaScript and native link interactions. No script splitting, workers, or scheduler code is warranted. Destination-page performance cannot be assessed because those pages are absent. |
+| Mobile interaction | The single-row navigation could overflow narrow viewports, with small link hit areas. The grid had a fixed 250px minimum. | Navigation wraps below 800px, links have a 44px minimum height, and the grid can shrink to the available width. All link destinations are preserved. |
+| Feedback | Links lacked a custom keyboard-focus treatment; hover transitions always ran. | Added visible focus outlines and respected reduced-motion preferences. Transitions affect color only. |
+| FCP / rendering | A small inline stylesheet and system fonts already avoid blocking CSS/font requests and font swaps. The DOM is small. | Retained this architecture. No CSS framework, font download, speculative prefetching, service worker, or rendering-containment machinery was added. |
+
+## Measured payloads
+
+The original Unsplash URL returned a 157,968-byte JPEG when downloaded for this audit. Its `auto=format` response can vary by client; this is a measured response, not a universal baseline.
+
+| Hero candidate | Dimensions | Bytes | Difference from measured original |
+| --- | --- | ---: | ---: |
+| Original remote image | 1350 × 900 | 157,968 | — |
+| Local WebP | 640 × 427 | 32,260 | 79.6% smaller |
+| Local WebP | 960 × 640 | 56,230 | 64.4% smaller |
+| Local WebP | 1350 × 900 | 100,138 | 36.6% smaller |
+| Local WebP | 1920 × 1280 | 186,470 | 18.0% larger, for higher-resolution displays |
+
+The browser chooses a candidate using viewport dimensions and device pixel ratio; a small high-density device may select a larger file. The 1920px option adds detail that the original 1350px image could not supply. The total asset directory size is not the per-page download size.
+
+HTML increased from 4,708 to 6,201 bytes (gzip: 1,735 to 2,186 bytes), mostly for responsive image markup and mobile styling. Runtime JavaScript and external font payloads remain zero. Rendering needs the HTML plus one hero image; no extra stylesheet or script request was introduced. Each image is under 200,000 bytes and the document is under 10,000 bytes uncompressed.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `pnpm dlx html-validate index.html` passed with no errors or warnings.
+- `git diff --check` passed.
+- Static checks confirmed every image URL exists, each file has a WebP signature, intrinsic widths match `srcset` descriptors, filenames match their SHA-256 content hashes, image dimensions and eager/high-priority attributes are present, and payloads fit the budgets above.
+- Compared every link destination against the original document; all are unchanged.
+- Confirmed there are no runtime scripts, iframes, remote resource URLs, or CSS imports in the page.
+
+These checks verify source and asset properties. They do **not** establish Lighthouse scores, actual LCP/INP/CLS, responsive visual correctness, server compression/cache behavior, or the behavior of linked routes. No browser measurements were performed, as requested.
+
+## Deployment and field follow-up
+
+Configure these at the production host, which is not defined in this repository:
+
+- Serve content-hashed files under `/assets/images/` with `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable`. Generate new hashes and update HTML whenever image contents change.
+- Serve HTML with revalidation, for example `Cache-Control: no-cache`, and Brotli or gzip compression. WebP files are already compressed.
+- Serve WebP as `image/webp`. Keep the assets on the same origin as the HTML.
+- Investigate production TTFB, redirects, CDN misses, and linked-route latency using hosting logs or production measurements; none can be inferred from these static files.
+
+When field data is available, assess the 75th percentile separately for mobile and desktop against LCP ≤ 2.5s, INP ≤ 200ms, and CLS ≤ 0.1. Use existing analytics or CrUX/PageSpeed Insights where available. Synthetic scores and real-user improvements are unmeasured in this audit.
+
+## Image provenance and maintenance
+
+Reused the site's existing [Unsplash stock photo](https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085); no new or generated artwork was introduced. Each local variant was downloaded from that endpoint with `fm=webp&fit=crop&w=WIDTH&q=60`, for widths 640, 960, 1350, and 1920. Filenames include the first ten hexadecimal characters of each file's SHA-256 digest. Image generation or optimization does not run during page requests.
+
+The implementation follows [web.dev's image priority guidance](https://web.dev/articles/fetch-priority) and [Core Web Vitals definitions](https://web.dev/articles/vitals); local modern-web-guidance guides `performance` and `optimize-image-priority` informed the changes.
